From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 007] fix: provide osmo_cpu_sched_vty_apply_localthread() off Linux as well

Patch 005 keeps cpu_sched_vty.c Linux only and adds a no-op
osmo_cpu_sched_vty_init() for the daemons that call it at startup. The
header declares a second public function, osmo_cpu_sched_vty_apply_localthread(),
which every worker thread of osmo-trx and osmo-bts calls to pick up its
per-thread policy from the cpu-sched node. It was left out, so linking
osmo-trx-uhd fails:

  Undefined symbols for architecture arm64:
    "_osmo_cpu_sched_vty_apply_localthread", referenced from:
        async_event_loop(uhd_device*) in libdevice.a(UHDDevice.o)
        TxLowerLoopAdapter(Transceiver*) in libtransceiver_common.a(Transceiver.o)

Add it next to the initialiser, returning 0. That is also what the Linux
implementation returns when no configured policy matches the calling
thread, so callers see the same outcome as on a Linux host with no
cpu-sched block.
---
diff --git a/src/vty/cpu_sched_vty.c b/src/vty/cpu_sched_vty.c
index cf2c18a..51d3beb 100644
--- a/src/vty/cpu_sched_vty.c
+++ b/src/vty/cpu_sched_vty.c
@@ -703,4 +703,13 @@ int osmo_cpu_sched_vty_init(void *tall_ctx)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Called by every thread that osmo-trx and osmo-bts start, to apply the
+ * per-thread policy from the cpu-sched node. There is no node and nothing
+ * to apply, so report success, which is also what the Linux code returns
+ * when no policy matches the thread. */
+int osmo_cpu_sched_vty_apply_localthread(void)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
 #endif /* __linux__ */
